priority:
 into its XML template, and a uniform priority
  across every URL carries exactly as much information as none at all (Google
  ignores the attribute either way); and the plugin's  comes from the
  file mtime, which a CI checkout rewrites to the build time, stamping every
  entry with the same meaningless date. Here  is the last commit date
  for the source file, and is omitted when git cannot supply one.

  Exclusions are derived, not listed: anything the page itself marks `noindex`
  (thanks.html), and anything that is only a meta-refresh stub (the /hu/
  redirects, the /blog/ + author/category/tag stubs). Add a `Robots:` or
  `Redirect:` header to a page and it drops out of here automatically.

  The hand-authored microsites and essays are in sitemap-projects.xml.
#}

{% for page in pages %}
{% if 'noindex' not in (page.robots|default('')) and not page.redirect %}

    {{ SITEURL }}/{{ page.url }}
{% set lastmod = page.source_path | git_lastmod %}
{% if lastmod %}    {{ lastmod }}
{% endif %}    monthly

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% for article in articles %}

    {{ SITEURL }}/{{ article.url }}
{% set lastmod = article.source_path | git_lastmod %}
{% if lastmod %}    {{ lastmod }}
{% endif %}    monthly

{% endfor %}
